         Source: Catalogo_ATS.xls, sheet "TABLAS REFERENCIALES".
         Columns: B = Código a usar, C = Tipo Transacción, D = Tipo de Identificación, E
         = Fecha Inicio (serial), F = Fecha Fin (serial, '-' = open)
         Rows 24 to 43, one record per row, in source order.
         Record ids are suffixed with the 1-based position in that order,
         so ats_catalog_entry_<table>_<n> is row 24 + n - 1.
         Every value below was read from the cell named above; nothing is
         interpolated.
    -->
    <!--
      * description joins the two human-readable cells verbatim as
        "<Tipo Transacción> - <Tipo de Identificación>". No value is
        invented; the separator is presentation only.
      * transaction_type_codes holds the referred transaction-type code
        of the row only where the two names agree. FONDOS Y FIDEICOMISOS
        (C37:C39) and COMPROBANTES ANULADOS (C40) name no row of the
        referred tables, so the field is left empty rather than guessed.
        See readme/ROADMAP.md.
    -->
